<title>RUSSIA: Russia details monopolies decree.</title>
<headline>Russia details monopolies decree.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A decree issued by President Boris Yeltsin on Monday on restructuring natural monopolies approves government proposals on monopoly reform, the presidential press service said.</p>
<p>The decree asks the government to prepare a programme during the first half of this year for restructuring, privatising and strengthening state control of natural monopolies.</p>
<p>Natural monopolies are industries which by their nature have no competitors, such as gas and electricity, telecommunications and railways.</p>
<p>The decree also asks the government to ensure that this programme is coordinated among the different government organs.</p>
<p>Yeltsin has given First Deputy Prime Minister Boris Nemtsov special responsibility for restructuring the monopolies, seen by both Russian ministers and international advisers, such as the International Monetary Fund, as crucial to the success of economic reform in Russia.</p>
<p>Nemtsov was due to hold a news conference at 1 p.m. (0900 GMT) on the decree.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
